    "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate reported a net prior year reserve release of $128.216 million for 2024, representing 7.68% of its opening gross claims outstanding. This release was primarily driven by favorable claims development in the International Casualty, Motor, and Property Treaty books, which benefited from reductions in prior years' loss estimates. However, some areas experienced adverse development, notably in US Casualty, where further strengthening was required in parts of the portfolio due to social and economic inflationary pressures, litigation severity, and claims volatility. Additionally, Faraday's Aviation book saw adverse experience and increased cost reserves related to Russia/Ukraine litigations. The overall movement is a mix of releases and strengthenings across different lines of business.",
